# No duplicate implementations & shared boundary discipline

Never maintain parallel implementations of the same UI component, menu behavior, formatter, or service helper, and never leak consumer/route implementation details into shared systems (`apps/web/src/app/collage/`, `packages/ui/`, `packages/maps/`).

## Canonical implementations

### Collage UI and interactive controls

- **Typography:** `Typography` in `@dg/ui/core/Typography` (`variant` / `data-typography="<role>"`) and `apps/web/src/app/collage/typography.css` (never declare `font`, `font-family`, `font-size`, `font-weight`, `line-height`, or `letter-spacing` in route/component stylesheets, and never leak route or component class selectors into `typography.css`)
- **Cards, status cards, tags, buttons, and filter pills:** `PaperCard`, `PaperStatus`, `PaperTag`, `PaperButton`, `PaperPills`, `PaperStrip`, and `FilterBar` in `apps/web/src/app/collage/`
- **Sticky filter bars:** `FilterBar` (`variant="default" | "spread" | "start" | "stack"`) in `apps/web/src/app/collage/FilterBar.tsx` (never apply `.pillStrip` directly in route components or list route filter classes in `pills.css` / `chrome.css`)
- **Dropdown and hover menus:** `HoverMenu`, `PillMenu`, `PillMenuList`, `PillMenuOption`, and `YearMenu` in `apps/web/src/app/collage/PillMenu.tsx` and `apps/web/src/app/collage/YearMenu.tsx` (never wire `bindHoverMenu` or `<details className="chrome__music">` directly in route or layout components)
- **Cutouts, seals, tickets, and stamps:** `CutOut`, `CutLetters`, and `scallopVertices` in `apps/web/src/app/collage/`, plus `Scallop` (`size="seal" | "sticker"`) and `Stub` (`kind="ticket" | "stamp"`, `size="default" | "compact" | "sm" | "xs"`) in `apps/web/src/app/music/stats/StatsShapes.tsx`
- **Side project marks:** `SideProjectMark` in `apps/web/src/app/home/GatteySitesCard.tsx`
- **Loading skeletons:** `Skeleton` in `@dg/ui/core/Skeleton` (never define route-local `SkeletonLine` components or raw `data-skeleton` elements)
- **Images and CDN image loader:** `Image` in `@dg/ui/dependent/Image` and `imageLoader` in `apps/web/src/utils/imageLoader.ts` (never import `next/image` directly in route components)
- **Maps:** `@dg/maps` (`MapCard`, `RoutePrint`, `RoutePeek`, `RouteAtlasMap`)
- **Spotify playback status:** `PlaybackStatus` in `apps/web/src/app/spotify/PlaybackStatus.tsx`

### Formatters and dates

- **Relative time and hydration-safe clock:** `RelativeTime` in `@dg/ui/core/RelativeTime` and `useServerTime` / `useNow` in `@dg/ui/core/ServerTimeContext`
- **Integer counts and distances:** `formatCount`, `formattedDistance`, and `METERS_PER_MILE` in `@dg/shared-core/formatting/formattedDistance`, plus Strava unit helpers (`formatMiles`, `formatFeet`, `formatCompactFeet`, `formatHours`, `formatDuration`, `formatOutingDay`, `formatOutingDate`) in `apps/web/src/app/activities/stravaFormat.ts`
- **Calendar buckets, year ticks (`’17`), and UTC short dates (`Oct 15, 2024` / `Oct 15`):** `periodStatus`, `SITE_TIME_ZONE`, `formatYearTick`, and `formatUtcShortDate` in `@dg/shared-core/dates/periodStatus`

### Auth, OAuth, and service helpers

- **Constant-time string comparison and dev console auth:** `timingSafeEqualStrings` in `@dg/services/auth/devConsoleBasicAuth` and `isDevConsoleAccessAllowed` in `apps/web/src/auth/vercel/session.ts`
- **Cron Bearer authentication:** `isCronAuthorized` in `apps/web/src/app/api/apiResponses.ts`
- **OAuth token validation and persistence:** `validateSpotifyTokenResponse` in `@dg/services/spotify/spotifyClient`, `validateRawDataToToken` in `@dg/services/strava/stravaClient`, and `upsertAndCacheToken` in `@dg/services/clients/refreshedAccessToken`

## No consumer leakage in shared systems

1. **Zero route-specific selectors in shared stylesheets (`no-consumer-selectors-in-shared-css`):**
   - Shared stylesheets (`apps/web/src/app/collage/*.css`, `packages/**/*.css`) must never reference route-specific class prefixes (`.stats__*`, `.strava__*`, `.streets__*`, `.reading__*`, `.changelog__*`, `.music__*`, `.home__*`, `.siteMap__*`, `.devConsole__*`, `.error__*`).
   - Instead, expose a shared component or `variant` / `size` prop (e.g. `<FilterBar variant="spread">`, `<Typography variant="stat-lg">`, `<Stub size="sm">`, `<PaperStatus>`) and style the shared data attribute or class in one place.
2. **Zero route-specific imports or classes in shared components (`no-consumer-leakage-in-shared-component`):**
   - Shared components in `apps/web/src/app/collage/`, `packages/ui/`, and `packages/maps/` must never import from route directories (`../music/`, `../activities/`, `../reading/`, `../changelog/`, `../site-map/`, `../dev-console/`, `../home/`) or render route-specific class names. Route-specific components and stylesheets belong inside their route directory (`apps/web/src/app/<route>/`).

## Rules when refactoring or adding features

1. **Extend the canonical module instead of copying it.** If a route needs a new option on `FilterBar`, `Stub`, `Scallop`, `Skeleton`, `HoverMenu`, or a formatter, add a `variant` or `size` prop to the shared implementation.
2. **Migrate callers and delete legacy code in the same PR.** Never leave an older component or helper alongside its replacement.
3. **Encode structural guards in `packages/cli/src/check-structure.ts`.** When unifying a recurring duplicate pattern or boundary rule, add a fast check in `@dg/cli` so `pnpm exec turbo check` blocks regressions in CI.
